# Timeline conformance corpus.
#
# One entry per line: `<kind> <relative path>`.
#
# The corpus is enumerated here rather than discovered by walking directories,
# because directory iteration is unreliable in the WASM and Android emulator
# lanes this corpus exists to serve, and because an explicit index turns an
# unreferenced fixture into a visible omission rather than a silent one.
#
# Kinds — the corpus holds more than one shape of artifact, and nothing in the
# files themselves says which is which:
#
#   document  A complete `pulp.timeline.project` envelope. Fully validated:
#             structural summary, interchange concept census, and serialize
#             idempotence, against a sibling `<path>.expect` manifest.
#   fragment  A single entity envelope (not a project), used for entity-level
#             migration tests. Declared so it is accounted for; entity-level
#             validation is not yet implemented, so it is reported as skipped
#             rather than silently ignored.
#   payload   A raw byte blob that is never parsed as timeline JSON — it is
#             embedded as OpaqueContent to prove unknown content round-trips
#             byte for byte. Deliberately never decoded.
#
# Regenerate document manifests with:
#   pulp-fixture-runner --corpus <dir> --update
#
# A new schema version must add fixtures here. Keep entries grouped by version.

document v1/minimal.json
document v1/track.json
document v1/note-content.json
document v1/track-opaque.json
document v2/device-chain.json
document v3/automation-lane.json
document v4/sequence-markers.json

fragment v4/sequence-before-scenes.json

payload v1/unknown-content-envelope.json
